## 3. Target Audience & Searcher Profile

The primary searcher is a renter currently living in the Charlotte-Mecklenburg area (or planning to relocate there) who earns a low to moderate income and suspects they may qualify for rental assistance or reduced-rent housing. This includes working adults earning below 80% of the Area Median Income, families facing rent burden (spending more than 30% of income on housing), and seniors on fixed incomes. They are in the **discovery to comparison stage**: they have heard these programs exist but do not fully understand how AMI thresholds work, which programs apply to their situation, or what the application process involves. They expect a clear, jargon-free explanation of program types, specific eligibility numbers, and actionable next steps, not a brochure or a government portal navigation maze.

